Fill the stsd entries of the stream mov_read_stsd() set up.

Since a6e9b539f7 (2026-11-01) mov_read_stsd() picks the stream with get_curr_st(), which for
a HEIF item property (ipma -> ipco -> stsd) is the item's stream, and sizes that stream's
extradata arrays by the entry count. ff_mov_read_stsd_entries() still takes the last stream
and bumps its stsd_count, so the two disagree; mov_free_stream_context() then frees
sc->extradata[i] for i up to a stsd_count larger than the array (heap-buffer-overflow at
mov.c:10924 on close). Use get_curr_st() in ff_mov_read_stsd_entries() too. rtpdec_qt sets
trak_index/cur_item_id so get_curr_st() still returns its stream.
Not fixed upstream as of 50276fac71 (2026-11-23).

Includes libavformat/tests/heif_item_stsd.c (fate-heif-item-stsd): a HEIF meta box reduced from
a fuzzer input, with a two-entry stsd in ipco associated through ipma. Without the fix closing
the demuxer reads past the extradata arrays; this is reported under AddressSanitizer or
valgrind, a plain build may pass.

Upstream: none found; regression from a6e9b539f7 (PR FFmpeg/FFmpeg#25671, fixes #24931).

